# Arabelle travelling with the party (docs/voice/arabelle.md): short lines a guest says while walking with the party, shown and voiced
# like banter (story/banter.gd). The node's name says when it may play: quest_ on entering an area while their story is
# at that point (these come first), place_ on entering an area, fight_ after a won fight, idle_ now and then on the
# road. Each plays once per playthrough, only while Arabelle is with the party. Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ place_lake
if guest:arabelle and region:lake_zarovich
interject guest:arabelle: This is where the fisherman put me in the sack. The water was cold. It'll be cold for him too, one day.
endif
-> END

~ place_camp
if guest:arabelle and at:vallaki_vistani_camp
interject guest:arabelle: Papa will shout, then hug me, then shout again. I've already counted.
endif
-> END

~ place_castle
if guest:arabelle and region:castle_ravenloft
interject guest:arabelle: I've seen this room before. Not with my eyes. I don't like the next room. We should go to it anyway.
endif
-> END

~ place_vallaki
if guest:arabelle and region:vallaki
interject guest:arabelle: Somebody in this town is lying about a festival. Everybody is, really. But one of them more.
endif
-> END

~ fight_longer
if guest:arabelle
interject guest:arabelle: You took longer than last time. That's all right.
endif
-> END

~ fight_trip
if guest:arabelle
interject guest:arabelle: I knew which of you would trip. I didn't say, because it was funny.
endif
-> END

~ fight_nobody
if guest:arabelle
interject guest:arabelle: Nobody died. I knew they wouldn't. I don't always know.
endif
-> END

~ idle_wedding
if guest:arabelle
interject guest:arabelle: One of you is going to cry at a wedding. It isn't a happy one. You'll cry anyway.
endif
-> END

~ idle_feet
if guest:arabelle
interject guest:arabelle: I don't mind walking. My feet will be big when I'm grown. I've seen them.
endif
-> END

~ idle_white_dress
if guest:arabelle
interject guest:arabelle: The man in the castle dreams about a lady in a white dress. He's going to be very disappointed.
endif
-> END
